{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run/draft && cat > update.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Fifth turn: the fixed experiment ran as CheckRun 18e0d44919ed4eb786f1231efbab552c (status completed, tests_passed, exit_code 0, changed_target_files empty) and its parsed result comparison 0 is violated by witness event index 4, so the earlier conditional/unresolved account is replaced by a violated conclusion and an asserted defect claim scoped to the captured snapshot's log-update construction. The prerequisites correlated (admission alias takeover_ready matched at event index 3), so the witness event is emitted from the state the question is about: the responder holds compacted_idx 6 while the preparing node reports decided_idx 3 / accepted_idx 6, and the responder's handling aborts with 'attempt to subtract with overflow' instead of completing.\\\",\n  \\\"interpretations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"b2606c6f3c1148c5af396ef701166e6f-question-0\\\",\n      \\\"experiment_id\\\": \\\"8cb68564d0514352a61204d7c6be6f3c-experiment\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"follower_prepare\\\",\n        \\\"logsync\\\",\n        \\\"memstorage_suffix\\\",\n        \\\"storage_get_suffix_contract\\\",\n        \\\"sync_log\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"executions\\\": {\n        \\\"18e0d44919ed4eb786f1231efbab552c\\\": [4]\n      },\n      \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"violated\\\",\n      \\\"defect_claim\\\": \\\"asserted\\\",\n      \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n        {\n          \\\"entry_id\\\": \\\"b2606c6f3c1148c5af396ef701166e6f-knowledge-0\\\",\n          \\\"revision\\\": 1,\n          \\\"assertion\\\": \\\"with snapshots disabled the log update is built as get_suffix(common_prefix_idx) with no comparison against the responder's own compacted index\\\"\n        },\n        {\n          \\\"entry_id\\\": \\\"b2606c6f3c1148c5af396ef701166e6f-knowledge-1\\\",\n          \\\"revision\\\": 1,\n          \\\"assertion\\\": \\\"MemoryStorage::get_suffix(from) subtracts trimmed_idx unchecked and panics with overflow checks enabled for from < trimmed_idx\\\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Current account: in the captured snapshot, a follower handling a Prepare builds its log update from the preparing leader's decided index whenever that leader's accepted round is older, and for a non-snapshot Entry type it does so through get_suffix(common_prefix_idx) without comparing that index to its own compacted index. The retained run reaches exactly that state and shows the failure: three nodes decide three entries, all three accept three more while one node is kept below decided 3 (accepted_idx 6, decided_idx 3), the leader trims to 6 (legal: every node accepted 6) so the healthy follower's compacted_idx becomes 6 while the stale node misses the forwarded Compaction::Trim, the leader is then removed and the healthy follower becomes the accepted leader under ballot n=2, and the stale node's try_become_leader makes it prepare with decided_idx 3 / accepted_idx 6. CheckRun 18e0d44919ed4eb786f1231efbab552c parses six events; the admission alias takeover_ready matches event 3 (healthy_follower_is_leader true, healthy_follower_compacted_idx 6, stale_node_decided_idx 3, stale_node_accepted_idx 6), and the result event 4 records outcome 'aborted_panic' with panic_message 'attempt to subtract with overflow' at omnipaxos_storage/src/memory_storage.rs:103 while healthy_follower_compacted_idx is still 6. The declared predicate 'outcome == completed' is therefore contradicted by a complete witness with correlated prerequisites. Responsibility in this snapshot is shared and both parts are captured code: the core chooses the below-compaction prefix (legal under the Storage trait, which specifies returning an empty vector when entries do not exist for the interval, so the request itself is permitted) and MemoryStorage::get_suffix violates that contract by computing from - trimmed_idx unchecked, aborting the node. The observable consequence for the cluster is availability loss on a legal recovery/compaction/election sequence: the surviving healthy follower dies while handling an ordinary Prepare, and the takeover cannot be evaluated.\\\",\n      \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n        \\\"The aborting arithmetic is in the captured MemoryStorage implementation, not in the core crate: the core's call is legal per the Storage::get_suffix contract, so this witness proves the captured snapshot fails this path, not that the core's prefix choice is itself a contract violation.\\\",\n        \\\"Scoping: for a snapshot-capable Entry type the same Prepare takes the snapshot branch (decided_idx 6 > common_prefix_idx 3) and the suffix is then read at the responder's own decided index, so the failure observed here is specific to entries without snapshots (or to decided_idx <= common_prefix_idx); the run does not show a snapshot-capable variant failing.\\\",\n        \\\"The stale state is produced by dropping whole messages of one kind addressed to one node (decisions while it must stay at decided 3, then AcceptSync after it must promise without accepting); that is ordinary message loss under the target's fault model, and the state it produces (accepted 6 / decided 3 / older accepted round with the durable log intact) is what a crash-recovered node legitimately holds, but the drops are part of the harness's construction rather than of a natural crash alone.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"limitations\\\": [\n        \\\"Only the dev profile was measured (overflow checks enabled, as in the controller's cargo test invocation); the consequence when overflow checks are off is not observed, so no claim is made here about a silently wrong log update in that configuration.\\\",\n        \\\"The captured memory storage backend was used; whether the persistent storage backend also reaches a failing endpoint for the same request, and which endpoint, was not measured.\\\",\n        \\\"The witness is a single deterministic schedule of one cluster size (three nodes, majority quorum, batch_size 3, NoSnapshot entries, trim index 6); the account is scoped to that exercised configuration.\\\",\n        \\\"The panic aborts handling before any reply is produced, so the run witnesses the abort itself; the further cluster-level consequences (a stalled or inconsistent log) are not measured by this execution.\\\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\nJSON\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_19-20-29-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
